     computed to `text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .44px`. The lead
     paragraph — a full sentence of explanatory prose — rendered as "RELATIONSHIPS ARE THE
     CONNECTIONS IN YOUR SCHEMA: LINKS, FORMULAS, ROLLUPS…".

     The cause is structural, not a bad rule: this card is a DOM DESCENDANT of the Status `<th>`,
     because Oleh put the legend in the header on purpose. `text-transform`, `letter-spacing` and
     `font-weight` all INHERIT, so the 11px/700/uppercase column band flows straight into a
     290px card of body copy. It predates the vessel — the hand-written `.rl-tbl thead th` carried
     the same `text-transform: uppercase` — so this is a defect the migration REVEALED rather than
